Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Rootstock Swallows the Horn
- Story & Context: During an impenetrable sunrise pea-souper at Pier 14, Nia Vance wired her oboe into the harbor's emergency siren horn to warn an unguided grain freighter creeping dangerously close to the greenhouse barge. The piercing double-reed wail startled the ship’s pilot into blasting its reciprocal foghorn so violently that the concussion rattled thousand-dollar vanilla seedlings down into the bilge water. Jax grabbed the microphone and looped the passing hull’s low mechanical diesel rumble directly into his 909 sampler, screaming across the deck, "The mist can claim the channel, but the woodwind owns the tide!" The resulting impromptu groove turned a near-catastrophic maritime collision into an ecstatic, six-hour open-air pontoon rave.
